    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d373">

                <pb facs="0458" n="1292" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/674</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-22T18:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 24, 9.50
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3001. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 1723. Referring to your No. 1444, Department’s 2279, October 18, 5 p.m.
                    Before signing this undertaking I think I should call your attention to my
                    letter of June 18 [<hi rendition="#italic">September 19</hi>], No. 5418,<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d373-f1"/> second page, under caption of purchase of 2,000,000
                    tons. I think it is important to have an understanding as to whether subsequent
                    sales of iron ore should apply (1) in relief proportionately of the engagement
                    of the three Associated Governments or (2) to relieve the share in the total
                    liability of say one of the Associated Governments who might purchase for their
                    own account or make a sale. I am awaiting signing the undertakings, text of
                    which was telegraphed, until the foregoing point is cleared up.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
